    "surfBiteStatus": "current",
    "surfBiteReport": "As of July 31, 2026, the surf zone along the Panama City Beach / South Walton Emerald Coast corridor has been the bright spot in an otherwise storm-affected week. Water clarity remains stained following Tropical Storm Bertha, but pompano have been feeding actively in the surf despite the murky conditions, with reports of good catches continuing to build. Hardhead catfish are mixed in throughout, but anglers who locate the pompano schools are landing multiple fish per outing. The most productive bait combination has been shrimp or sand fleas tipped with Fishbites or Fish Gum; live sand fleas have been scarce so blanched fleas are the recommended alternative. With high tide falling during the late morning, an early-morning start is advised to hit the best tidal window, and anglers should re-scout familiar stretches for storm-reshaped sandbars and cuts before fishing.",
    "surfBiteSource": "Half Hitch PCB Fishing Report (2026-07-31)",
    "surfBiteSourceUrl": "https://halfhitch.com/blog/pcb-fishing-report-7-31-26",
